  "deck": "Jordan Henderson's 16 points led a Bin XI that scored 83, more than any side in the league.",
  "body": "Jordan Henderson is the find. Two goals and an assist from midfield in Chelsea's 5-1 dismantling of AFC Bournemouth, with three clearances and an interception for those who like their midfielders honest. Nothing in the bins came near it.\n\nIpswich Town supply a defence that scores: Dara O'Shea and Abdoul Ouattara each found the net in the 2-1 win over Fulham, with Olivier Boscagli's clean sheet in Brighton & Hove Albion's 2-0 against Sunderland beside them and Konstantinos Tzolakis making four saves in Hull City's 2-2 with Everton. Crystal Palace give the middle its spine, Jefferson Lerma scoring and Quinten Timber providing in the 3-1 over Nottingham Forest, with Jack Rudoni scoring for Coventry City in the 4-1 against Newcastle United. Up front Joe Gelhardt scored and Sorba Thomas provided for Hull, and Jorgen Strand Larsen set one up for Palace.",
